    "note": "The statement makes the name due where the payee differs from the seller. This rule asks for the name of every payee group the document carries, which is the same thing wherever the group is there at all: a payee group that repeats the seller carries no information, and the official artefacts additionally compare the two names. That comparison is left out here because two parties that spell one name are not thereby one party."
