      ]
    },
    "message": "The payment card primary account number (BT-87) at {@/BT-87} is {/BT-87}, which shows more than ten digits of the card number; at most the first six and the last four may be shown.",
    "source": "EN 16931-1, 6.4.1, Table 3, BR-51",
    "note": "The statement names the digits that may be shown, which is at most six at the front and four at the back, and this rule counts the digits of the value and asks for at most ten of them. The official validation artefacts ask instead that the whole value be at most ten characters long, which faults a number masked to its last four digits — sixteen characters of which twelve are asterisks — although such a number shows four digits and satisfies the statement. The two readings differ on a masked number, the norm is followed here, and the ledger records it."
